WEBVTT
Kind: subtitles
Language: en

1
00:00.230 --> 00:06.600
So we've talked a lot about all the different benefits and the power
of adopting a structured approach to problem solving.

2
00:06.600 --> 00:14.680
You save more time. You're much more deliberate about your approach.
You know exactly where you are in the process. There are many other benefits.

3
00:14.920 --> 00:19.600
But I'm curious, Marc: do you always take
the same structured approach to solving problems?

4
00:19.600 --> 00:23.200
No, it definitely varies depending upon the context.

5
00:23.200 --> 00:31.960
In some cases — if we're doing a new product introduction, for example — it might be
a design-thinking approach. If there is a lot of data involved, it might be an advanced-analytics approach.

6
00:32.040 --> 00:36.800
Generally, there are five different approaches
we typically see in problem solving.

7
00:36.800 --> 00:42.200
There is the hypothesis-led approach, which we're going
to go into a lot more detail on in this course.

8
00:42.200 --> 00:47.040
But there are also many others. There is the domain-IP-led approach.
There's the advanced-analytics approach.

9
00:47.300 --> 00:55.400
There's the design-thinking approach, and there's the engineering approach.
And depending upon the context of the problem, one approach may be better than another.

10
00:55.400 --> 01:01.980
And then I think another point is, you don't always just use one approach.
Again, depending upon the context, sometimes it's the combination of different approaches

11
01:02.120 --> 01:06.200
which would get you to the right answer —
or, in some cases, the answer more quickly.

12
01:06.200 --> 01:14.400
I love what you said, Marc, because I actually think what is super interesting
is that these five different problem-solving approaches,

13
01:14.400 --> 01:20.450
though the approaches might be a little bit different, their underlying characteristics
are all actually very similar. They all share some common characteristics.

14
01:20.770 --> 01:25.220
They all have a very focused problem statement.
They're all impact-oriented.

15
01:26.250 --> 01:32.230
They always take a stakeholder perspective. They're fact-based.
And they also focus on synthesis.

16
01:32.810 --> 01:38.240
These characteristics underpin every single one
of these different problem-solving approaches.
